	| Description | This is the default role for teams |
	| Name        | Default Team Role                  |
	| Type        | Team                               |
	And I delete a contact role on koroneiki with the name "Default Team Role"
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Team Role"

Scenario: View contact role audit entries
	Koroneiki contact role changes via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I update a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |
	Then I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Add" to the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role" field "Name" from the old value "" to the new value "Default Account Customer Role" executed by "Koroneiki QA Service Producer"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Update" to the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role" field "Name" from the old value "Default Account Customer Role" to the new value "Optional Account Customer Role" executed by "Koroneiki QA Service Producer"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Add" to the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role" field "Name" from the old value "" to the new value "Default Account Customer Role" executed by "Koroneiki QA Service Producer"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Update" to the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role" field "Name" from the old value "Default Account Customer Role" to the new value "Optional Account Customer Role" executed by "Koroneiki QA Service Producer"

Scenario: View contact role audit entries executed by agent
	Koroneiki contact role changes via API via an agent should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Agent Name  | Koroneiki User                                 |
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I update a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values
	| Agent Name  | Koroneiki User                                  |
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |
	Then I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Add" to the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role" field "Name" from the old value "" to the new value "Default Account Customer Role" executed by "Koroneiki User"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Update" to the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role" field "Name" from the old value "Default Account Customer Role" to the new value "Optional Account Customer Role" executed by "Koroneiki User"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Add" to the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role" field "Name" from the old value "" to the new value "Default Account Customer Role" executed by "Koroneiki User"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Update" to the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role" field "Name" from the old value "Default Account Customer Role" to the new value "Optional Account Customer Role" executed by "Koroneiki User"

Scenario: View contact role audit entries executed by admin and agent
	Koroneiki contact role changes via API via an agent and admin should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I update a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values
	| Agent Name  | Koroneiki User                                  |
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |
	Then I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Add" to the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role" field "Name" from the old value "" to the new value "Default Account Customer Role" executed by "Koroneiki QA Service Producer"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Update" to the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role" field "Name" from the old value "Default Account Customer Role" to the new value "Optional Account Customer Role" executed by "Koroneiki User"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Add" to the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role" field "Name" from the old value "" to the new value "Default Account Customer Role" executed by "Koroneiki QA Service Producer"
	And I should be able to view an audit entry for an action "Update" to the contact role "Optional Account Customer Role" field "Name" from the old value "Default Account Customer Role" to the new value "Optional Account Customer Role" executed by "Koroneiki User"

Scenario: Create and view contact role external link
	Koroneiki account external link created by contact roles via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I create an external link for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" with the following values
	| Domain      | contactrole |
	| Entity Id   | 1234        |
	| Entity Name | ContactRole |
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" and domain "contactrole" should be present on the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" with the following values
	| Domain      | contactrole |
	| Entity Id   | 1234        |
	| Entity Name | ContactRole |

Scenario: Remove and view contact role external link
	Koroneiki contact role external links removed via API should not be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I create an external link for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" with the following values
	| Domain      | contactrole |
	| Entity Id   | 1234        |
	| Entity Name | ContactRole |
	And I delete an external link with the entity id "1234" on the contact role "Default Account Customer Role"
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should not be present on the contact role "Default Account Customer Role"